I've been playing wizards, trying to get a "fast" ascension.  This was my
fastest yet, though I realize it's far from _the_ fastest.  I found a magic
lamp just after turn 1000 in minetown, and wished for speed boots (never
found any others).  Later (turn 2500 or so) I found some Gauntlets of Power.
I got scales from a Silver Dragon in the castle.

I used the castle wand, which was found at (0:2) for the Bag of Holding
(never found any others), a magic marker, a spellbook of FoD, and 4 wishes
for "3 cursed potions of gain level".  The first such wish gave me 3
potions, but each of the wand's last three wishes gave me only 1 potion.

I used Wes Irby's trick of descending into the Sanctum (dlvl 48), climbing
back up, and using a cursed scroll of teleport to get near the inner
sanctum, saving many turns wading through the sanctum's throngs of monsters
and bugs.  The wizard appeared and double-troubled in the high-priest's room
and I realized I needed the FoD spell, so I drank one of my precious c!GL to
return to VS level (dlvl 47), wished for and read the +FoD, wrote one more
c?Teleport, returned to the sanctum with "the trick" again.  I fingered the
high priest and one of the Rodneys, whereupon Rodney double-troubled again,
but I quickly fingered both of them, too.

On the climb out of Gehennom, I used the cursed potions of gain level in
each demons lair.  I was thrown back a handful of times, but never had to
redo a demon's lair, which was helpful.

Genociding wouldn't have saved me much time, and poly-piling would have
slowed me *way* down.

One of these days, I'd like to ascend in less than 10K turns, but, alas, not
this time.

